Vitamin A deficiency is a major health problem in parts of the world where children have a limited diet. Rice enhanced with pro-vitamin A has been produced through genetic engineering. This new rice, called Golden Rice, contains large amounts of $\beta$-carotene, which is used in the human body to synthesise vitamin A. From this Golden Rice, newer varieties of Golden Rice have been developed by selective breeding.

Fig. 3.1 shows how Golden Rice was originally produced by genetic engineering.

